  cup_structure:
    border: 8-connected single-color component (5-17 pixels), unique color per cup
    shape: hollow frame converging to a single-pixel tail tip on one bbox edge and open on the opposite edge. Shapes vary widely — symmetric funnels/Ys, asymmetric Ys (one arm noticeably shorter than the other), and irregular zigzag/staircase frames all occur. Do NOT assume two equal-length arms.
    tail: one bbox edge containing exactly 1 border pixel (the spike); this is the edge from which content is ejected. Other bbox edges may have any count ≥1. (When several bbox edges happen to share count 1, the solver picks among them deterministically — see solver for the disambiguation rule.)
    bbox: 3-8 rows x 3-7 cols
    mouth_interior: the cup's hollow interior — the non-border cells lying within the frame's enclosed region. Excludes bbox corners that fall outside the frame. At least 3 cells required.
  content:
    color: single non-bg color different from own border; may match other cups' border/content
    count: 1-7 pixels scattered strictly inside mouth_interior (never in bbox corners outside the walled region)
    density: 10-45% of mouth-interior cells [observed]
